Multiplying both sides by $x^3$,

\begin{align*} x^3 \cdot \frac{1}{(x-2)^2} &= x^3 \cdot \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} n \cdot (-x+3)^{n-1}\\ \frac{x^3}{(x-2)^2} &= \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} n \cdot x^3 \cdot (-x+3)^{n-1} \end{align*}

